  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Commonwealth of Massachusetts has recorded $217M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buying agency with $110M in obligations, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $36.3M and the Department of Transportation with $29.7M. Federal obligations are down 99.1% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years, and the current-year total is a partial fiscal year to date. Federal award activity in Massachusetts includes 7,373 awards with an average award size of $29.4K. Historical annual obligations show much larger totals in recent full years: FY22 was $18.4B, FY23 was $20.3B, FY24 was $19B, FY25 was $21.4B, and FY26 was $23.5B. Top vendor recipients in FY2027 to date include CRANE & CO., INC. at $36M and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $14.4M. Leading industries by NAICS include Paper Mills at $34M and Engineering Services at $26.7M. These figures reflect obligations only and represent fiscal year to date totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is federal contracting in Massachusetts right now?",
        "body": "Massachusetts has $217M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Massachusetts has 7,373 awards so far and an average award size of $29.4K. Massachusetts obligations are down 99.1% year over year. Massachusetts totals for prior full fiscal years were $18.4B in FY22, $20.3B in FY23, $19B in FY24, $21.4B in FY25, and $23.5B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and suppliers in Massachusetts this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer at $110M, followed by the Department of the Treasury at $36.3M and the Department of Transportation at $29.7M. The largest vendors are CRANE & CO., INC. at $36M and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $14.4M, with PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC and KMK CONSTRUCTION, INC each at $11.8M. The largest industries are Paper Mills at $34M and Engineering Services at $26.7M."
      }
    ]
